# Installing @PLUGIN_NAME@ (v@PLUGIN_VERSION@)

**@PLUGIN_NAME@** by @COMPANY_NAME@. Formats: **AU** (Mac) and **VST3** (Mac + Windows).
Not available as AAX (Pro Tools) or standalone.

---

## Mac (macOS 11 Big Sur or newer, Apple Silicon and Intel)

### 1. Copy the plugin files

Unzip the download, then open Finder and choose **Go → Go to Folder…** to reach each folder:

| File | Copy it to |
|---|---|
| `@PLUGIN_NAME@.component` | `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components` |
| `@PLUGIN_NAME@.vst3` | `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3` |

### 2. Let macOS open it (one time)

@PLUGIN_NAME@ isn't sold through the App Store, so macOS flags it as "downloaded from the
internet" and DAWs may refuse to load it or say it's **damaged**. It isn't damaged. Clear the
flag with either option:

**Option A: Terminal (recommended, works for every DAW)**

Open **Terminal** (Cmd+Space, type *Terminal*, press Return), paste this line, press Return:

```
xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/Components/"@PLUGIN_NAME@".component ~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/VST3/"@PLUGIN_NAME@".vst3; killall -9 AudioComponentRegistrar 2>/dev/null; echo done
```

**Option B: Open Anyway (no Terminal)**

If macOS shows *"Apple could not verify @PLUGIN_NAME@ is free of malware"* when your DAW scans it:
click **Done**, open **System Settings → Privacy & Security**, scroll down, and click
**Open Anyway** next to the @PLUGIN_NAME@ message. Then rescan in your DAW.
(The right-click → Open trick only works for apps, not plugin files, so use this or Option A.)

### 3. Rescan in your DAW

- **Logic Pro / GarageBand:** Settings → Plug-in Manager → select @PLUGIN_NAME@ → **Reset & Rescan Selection**.
  It's under **Audio Units → @COMPANY_NAME@**.
- **FL Studio:** Options → Manage plugins → **Find installed plugins**. Use the VST3 or AU.
- **Ableton Live:** Settings → Plug-Ins → enable AU / VST3 system folders → **Rescan**.
- **Others:** rescan plug-ins in your DAW's settings.

---

## Windows (10 or 11, 64-bit)

1. Right-click the zip → **Properties** → tick **Unblock** if you see it → OK. Then **Extract All**.
2. Copy `@PLUGIN_NAME@.vst3` into `C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3`
   (it may look like a folder; copy the whole thing).
3. Rescan plug-ins in your DAW (FL Studio: Options → Manage plugins → **Find installed plugins**).

---

## Good to know

- **Window size:** click the small ≡ button in the bottom-right corner to pick 75 / 100 / 125 %.
- **Gag sounds** (comedy sound effects mixed into the audio) are **off by default** so they never
  end up in a mix by accident. Turn them on from the ≡ menu if you want them.
- **Presets** you save live in `Documents/@COMPANY_NAME@/@PLUGIN_NAME@`.

## Uninstall

Delete `@PLUGIN_NAME@.component` and `@PLUGIN_NAME@.vst3` from the folders above.

